$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM ((3E,5E)-7,7-dimethylocta-3,5-dien-1-yl)benzene (7d). Allylic phosphonate
6a (172 mg, 0.61 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF (2.4 mL, 0.25 M)
and cooled to -78 °C. NaHMDS (123 mg, 0.67 mmol, 1.1 equiv., 2.5 M in
hexanes) was added slowly. After 1 hour at -78 °C, pivaldehyde (99 μL,
0.92 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to the solution. After 15 minutes, the
reaction mixture was warmed up to rt and allowed to stir for 12 hours.
The reaction was then quenched by addition of aqueous NH4Cl solution and
the product was extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with
brine, dried over MgSO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The reaction
mixture was purified by column chromatography (grad. 0%→2% EtOAc in
hexanes). (72 mg, 0.34 mmol, 55%, 89:11 EE:Σ(other) by 1H NMR) as a
colorless oil. 1H NMR (700MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.3-7.27 (m, 2H), 7.23-7.17 (m,
3H), 6.06 (dd, J = 10.7, 15.2 Hz, 1H), 5.95 (dd, J = 10.2, 15.5 Hz, 1H),
5.67-5.60 (m, 2H), 2.71 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 2.39 (q, J = 8.0, 2H), 1.03
(s, 9H); 13C NMR (175 MHz, CDCl3) δ 144.0, 142.0, 131.3, 131.3, 128.4,
128.3, 125.8, 125.0, 35.9, 34.5, 33.0, 29.6; HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for
C16H22 [M]+ 214.1721, found 214.1719; IR (thin film, cm-1) 3025, 2959,
2929, 2904, 2864, 1496, 1476, 1461, 1454, 1361, 1270, 1258, 1030, 989,
745, 698.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (E:other=89:11), Horner-Wadsworth-Emmons reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

