$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Fluoroolefins 10; General Procedure.
Fluorinated BT-sulfone 7 (1.20 equiv) and aldehyde 9 (0.080-0.510 mmol,
1.00 equiv) were dissolved in anhyd THF (33 mL/mmol 9) at 0 °C. To the
mixture, LiHMDS (2.40 equiv) was added dropwise and stirred 1.5 h at 0
°C. The reaction was quenched with sat. aq NaHCO3 (10 mL/mmol 9) and
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 30 mL/mmol 9). The combined organic layers were
washed with brine (10 mL/mmol 9) and dried (Na3SO4). The solvent was
evaporated and the crude product was purified by column chromatography
(cHex-EtOAc). 4-[2-(2-Bromophenyl)-2-fluorovinyl]pyridine as a colorless
oil, yield 0.031 g, 0.112 mmol, 51%. Rf = 0.29 (cHex-EtOAc, 1:1). IR
(KBr): 3440, 3057, 2922, 2850, 1713, 1678, 1630, 1597, 1563, 1492, 1468,
1385, 1223, 1188, 1096, 1075, 1026, 992 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 6.12 (d, J = 36.7 Hz, 1 H, CH=CF), 6.48 (d, J = 17.8 Hz, 1 H, CHCF),
6.81 (d, J = 4.2 Hz, 2 Harom), 7.28-7.41 (m, 4 Harom), 7.50 (d, J = 4.1
Hz, 2 Harom), 7.55 (dd, J = 7.7, 1.5 Hz, 1 Harom), 7.66-7.74 (m, 3
Harom), 8.39 (br s, 2 Harom), 8.64 (br s, 2 Harom). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 109.4, 110.0, 121.5, 121.7, 127.5, 128.0, 128.3, 129.5,
130.7, 131.4, 131.8, 132.1, 133.6, 133.9, 140.6, 141.0, 149.7, 150.0,
151.1, 159.6, 160.2. 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -90.2, -80.7.MS (70
eV, EI): m/z (%) = 279/278/277 (42/7/42, [M+]), 199/198(14/100, [M -
Br+]), 170 (31). HR-EIMS: m/z calcd for C13H9BrFN: 279.9902; found:
279.9900.
