$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 19. To a solution of sulfone 6 (350 mg, 0.476 mmol) in 3 mL of
DMF/HMPA (3:1 v/v) was added LiHMDS (1.0 M in THF, 0.71 mL, 0.71 mmol) at
-40 °C. This was stirred for 10min and followed by the addition of
aldehyde 5 (316 mg, 0.952 mmol) in 2 mL of DMF/HMPA (3:1 v/v) via
cannula. The reaction was allowed to warm slowly to room temperature and
stirred for 24 h before it was diluted by the addition of brine. The
layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2.
The combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over NaSO4,
filtered, and concentrated. Purification on silica gel (hexanes) provided
19. Colorless oil, yield 200 mg, 50%. [α]24 D= -12.0 (c = 1.73, CHCl3);
IR (film): 3064, 3050, 2956, 2929, 2857, 2702, 1471, 1462, 1423, 1375,
1358, 1253, 1106, 834, 773 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.70-7.67 (m,
4H), 7.42-7.35 (m, 6H), 5.56-5.51 (m, 1H), 5.45 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H),
3.80 (m, 1H), 3.57 (m, 1H), 3.35 (s, 2H), 2.05-2.02 (m, 1H), 1.75-1.67
(m, 2H), 1.56-1.52 (m, 3H), 1.26 (s, 3H), 1.06 (s, 9H), 0.96 (d, J = 6.0
Hz, 3H), 0.93 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 0.91 (d, J = 4.2 Hz, 3H), 0.89 (s,
9H), 0.88 (s, 18H), 0.87 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 0.07 (s, 3H), 0.06 (s, 3H),
0.04 (s, 3H), 0.03 (s, 3H), -0.0 (s, 3H), -0.0 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 136.4, 136.0, 136.0, 135.3, 134.3, 129.6, 129.4, 128.3, 127.6,
127.4, 75.7, 75.1, 72.6, 71.6, 38.3, 37.2, 35.8, 34.4, 27.2, 26.0, 26.0,
24.5, 20.3, 19.4, 18.4, 18.3, 18.2, 15.3, 15.2, -2.0, -4.2, -4.3, -5.3;
MS (ESI): m/z 863.5, [M+Na]+;
