$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM β-parinaric acid. Phosphonate (267 mg, 0.74 mmol, 1 equv.) was dissolved
in THF (0.25 M) and cooled to -78 °C. NaHMDS (1.1 equiv., 1 M in hexanes)
was added slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C, trans-2-pentenal (109 μL,
1.11 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to the solution. After 15 minutes, the
reaction mixture was warmed up to rt and allowed to stir for 10 hours.
Added LiOH (177 mg, 7.4 mmol, 10 equiv.) as a solution in 1:1 H2O:MeOH (2
mL) and heated the reaction mixture to 50 °C for 5 hours. The reaction
was diluted with EtOAc and washed with 1M HCl. Extracted the aqueous
layer with EtOAc. The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried over Na2SO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The unpurified
reaction mixture was purified by column chromatography (grad. 0%→10%
ether/hexanes). 1H and 13C NMR matched previously reported assignments.
(99 mg, 0.36 mmol, 48%; 7:1 all-E:Σ(other isomers) by 1H NMR) as a white
solid. 1H NMR (700MHz, CDCl3) δ 10.64 (brs, 1 H), 6.20-6.11 (m, 4H),
6.10-6.04 (m, 2H), 5.73 (dt, J = 6.6, 14.2 Hz, 1H), 5.68 (dt, J = 7.1,
14.6 Hz, 1H), 2.35 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.15-2.07 (m, 4H), 1.67-1.60 (m,
2H), 1.43-1.18 (m, 8H), 1.01 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (175 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 179.0, 136.6, 135.0, 132.5, 132.4, 130.9, 130.8, 130.6, 129.6,
33.8, 32.8, 29.2, 29.1, 29.0, 28.9, 25.9, 24.6, 13.5; HRMS (EI) m/z calcd
for C18H28O2 [M]+ 276.2089, found 276.2095; IR (thin film, cm-1) 3011,
2960, 2919, 2848, 1711, 1460, 991.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective (E:other=7:1), Horner-Wadsworth-Emmons reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

