$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM A) Procedure Using KO-tBu
2-((4R,6S)-6-((Benzo[d]thiazol-2-ylsulfonyl)methyl)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxan-4-yl)acetate
sec-butyl ester (C, 8.0 g 18.1 mmol) and
N-(4-(4-fluorophenyl)-5-formyl-6-isopropylpyrimidin-2-yl)-N-methylmethanesulfonamide
(D, 6.4 g, 18.1 mmol) were added to 110 mL of tetrahydrofuran. The
mixture was heated until complete dissolution was obtained. The solution
was cooled to -50°C., followed by addition of 19.9 mL of 1 M KO-tBu in
tetrahydrofuran (19.9 mmol) in 1 h. The temperature was allowed to
increase to -10°C and quenched with 100 mL of 10 w/w % of aqueous NH4Cl.
HPLC analysis indicated 77% product formation. The layers were separated
and the organic phase washed again with 10 w/w % aqueous NH4Cl. Then the
reaction mixture was extracted three times with brine at a pH of 12-13
(adjusted with 4 M aqueous NaOH). After drying over Na2SO4, the organic
layer was evaporated to give an oil, which slowly solidified. The solid
was re-crystallized from isopropanol.
2-((4R,6S)-6-((E)-2-(4-(4-fluorophenyl)-6-isopropyl-2-(N-methylmethanesulfonamido)pyrimidin-5-yl)vinyl)-2,2-dimethyl-1,3-dioxan-4-yl)acetate,
sec-butyl ester (compound E) as a white solid (5.0 g, yield 48%). 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.58 (dd, 2H), 7.01 (t, 2H), 6.45 (dd, 1H), 5.40 (dd,
1H), 4.81, (m, 1H), 4.44-4.18 (m, 2H), 3.54-3.47 (m, 3H), 3.47-3.38 (m,
3H), 3.35-3.25 (m, 1H), 2.37 (ddd, 2H), 1.59-1.43 (m, 4H), 1.41 (s, 3H),
1.33 (s, 3H), 1.20, (dd, 6 H), 1.14 (d, 3H), 0.83 (t, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, first stage heated to dissolve reactants; second stage
slow addition; third stage quench; Julia-Kocienski olefination, key step
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Process for the preparation of statins by means of a Julia-Kocienski
reaction in the presence of metal alkoxy base
