$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl
2-((2R,6S)-6-((S,2E,4E)-7-((2R,3R)-3-((2S,3S)-3-((diethyl(isopropyl)silyl)oxy)-pentan-2-yl)oxiran-2-yl)-6-methylhepta-2,4-dien-2-yl)tetrahydro-2H-pyran-2-yl)acetate
(5). A stirred solution of sulfone 45 (30 mg, 0.13 mmol) in anhydrous THF
(1.0 mL) at -78 °C (bath temperature) was slowly treated with a solution
of KHMDS (0.42 mL, 0.21 mmol, 0.5 M in toluene). The resulting yellow
solution was allowed to stir for 1 h and then slowly treated with a
solution of aldehyde 16b (104 mg, 0.19 mmol) in anhydrous THF (1.0 mL).
This mixture was stirred at -78 °C for an hour and then quenched by the
addition of saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (1 mL). This mixture was
warmed to rt and then stirred for another 10 min. The resulting mixture
was extracted with EtOAc (3x10 mL) and washed with brine (5 mL). The
combined organic extracts were dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The resulting residue was purified on a silica column
(2-20% EtOAc in hexanes). 32 mg (46%) of diene (E:Z = 93:7) 5 as an oil.
1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.33 - 6.24 (m, 1H), 5.99 (ddd, J = 11.0, 2.2,
1.1 Hz, 1H), 5.54 (dd, J = 15.0, 8.2 Hz, 1H), 3.88 - 3.70 (m, 3H), 3.67
(s, 3H), 2.73 - 2.56 (m, 3H), 2.50 - 2.38 (m, 2H), 1.93 - 1.80 (m, 1H),
1.73 (d, J = 1.3 Hz, 3H), 1.71 - 1.56 (m, 4H), 1.56 - 1.44 (m, 4H), 1.38
- 1.19 (m, 3H), 1.06 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 3H), 1.04 - 0.96 (m, 13H), 0.93 -
0.89 (m, 1H), 0.88 - 0.77 (m, 6H), 0.73 - 0.57 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (101 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 171.8, 139.0, 136.7, 125.2, 124.3, 82.1, 74.4, 74.2, 61.1, 57.1,
51.5, 41.5, 39.9, 39.7, 35.3, 31.0, 29.6, 27.6, 23.5, 21.2, 17.4, 17.4,
13.5, 13.2, 9.8, 9.5, 7.2, 7.0, 4.2, 4.0; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for
C30H55O5Si (M+H)+ 523.3819, found 523.3832.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, key step, Julia-Kocienski Olefination, product obtained
as a mixture of 93:7 E:Z isomers
