$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Julia-olefination product – jerangolid A TBS-ether. To a -60 ºC solution
of PT-sulfone 23 (22 mg, 0.053 mmol) in a mixture of DMF (0.5 mL) and
HMPA (0.13 mL) was added LiHMDS (58 μL of a 1 M solution in hexanes,
0.058 mmol). After 20 min at that temperature, crude aldehyde 9 (26 mg,
0.087 mmol) was added in a solution of DMF (0.5 mL) and HMPA (0.13 mL).
The reaction mixture was stirred for two hours at -60 ºC, after which it
was allowed to slowly warm to 0 ºC. The mixture was subsequently diluted
with EtOAc and quenched by addition of saturated NH4Cl solution. The
organic phase was washed with water, brine, dried (Na2SO4), and
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by flash chromatography
(hexanes: EtOAc, 4:1 to 1:1) to give 12 mg (46%) of jerangolid TBS-ether
as a colorless oil (E/Z > 25:1 by 1H NMR of crude product). The product
TBS-ether was contaminated with some aromatic impurities from olefination
byproducts and used in the next step without further purification.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Julia olefination; E:Z >25:1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Total Synthesis of Jerangolid A
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hanessian, Stephen; Focken, Thilo; Oza, Rupal
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2010), 12(14), 3172-3175

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME72 STEP1
$RXN



