$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: diethyl
((2E,4E,6E)-7-phenylhepta-2,4,6-trien-1-yl)phosphonate (5h).
Sulfonylphosphonate 2e (227 mg, 0.57 mmol, 1 equiv.) was dissolved in THF
(2.3 mL, 0.25 M) and cooled to -78 °C. KHMDS (136 mg, 0.68 mmol, 1.2
equiv., 1 M in THF) was added slowly. After five minutes at -78 °C,
trans-cinnamaldehyde (0.11 mL, 0.85 mmol, 1.5 equiv.) was added to the
solution. After 20 minutes, the reaction mixture was warmed up to 0 °C.
After 1 hour, the reaction was quenched by addition of aqueous NH4Cl
solution and the product was extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was
washed with brine, dried over MgSO4, and then concentrated in vacuo. The
reaction mixture was purified by column chromatography (grad. 15%→30%
acetone in hexanes). (67 mg, 0.22 mmol, 39%, 62:38 EE:EZ by 1H NMR) as a
colorless oil. 1H NMR (700MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.39 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.31
(t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.22 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H), 6.80 (ddd, J = 5.0, 9.6,
15.7 Hz, 1H), 6.57 (d, J = 15.4 Hz, 1H), 6.36-6.33 (m, 2H), 6.27 (ddd, J
= 4.9, 9.9, 14.9 Hz, 1H), 5.70 (dt, J = 7.7, 15.3 Hz, 1H), 4.11 (m, 4H),
2.69 (dd, J = 7.7, 22.7 Hz, 2H), 1.32 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 6H); 13C NMR (175
MHz, CDCl3) δ 137.7, 135.1 (d, J = 15.3 Hz), 132.7 (d, J = 2.6 Hz), 132.7
(d, J = 4.8 Hz), 132.5 (d, J = 5.3 Hz), 128.8(d, J = 2.9 Hz), 128.6,
127.5, 126.3, 122.6 (d, J = 13.1 Hz), 62.0 (d, J = 6.8 Hz), 31.1 (d, J =
140.0 Hz), 16.5 (d, J = 5.9 Hz); HRMS (ES) m/z calcd for C17H23O3P [M+H]+
307.1458, found 307.1463; IR (thin film, cm-1) 3023, 2985, 2929, 2906,
1597, 1491, 1448, 1392, 1368, 1295, 1243, 1161, 1097, 1027, 965, 864,
838, 814, 785, 752, 695.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective (EE:EZ=62:38), alternative preparation
shown, Julia-Kocienski olefination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of conjugated polyenes via sequential condensation of
sulfonylphosphonates and aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cichowicz, Nathan R.; Nagorny, Pavel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(4), 1058-1061

