$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S,E)-methyl
8-(2-(3-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)pent-1-enyl)-5-oxocyclopent-1-
enyl)octanoate, 19a. The reaction was carried out employing Barbier type
conditions. A solution of sulfone 11 (81, 0.21 mmol) in 2 mL of anhydrous
THF was transferred via cannula under nitrogen to a stirred solution of
the aldehyde 10a (51 mg, 0.19 mmol) in 2.5 mL of anhydrous THF, and the
resulting mixture was cooled to -78 ºC. Then, 460 μL of KHMDS (0.5 M in
Toluene, 0.22 mmol) were added at this temperature and, after 10 min, the
reaction mixture was warmed to room temperature and stirred for 2h. After
completion of the reaction, the mixture was quenched with 4 mL of aqueous
saturated NH4Cl solution. After a few minutes of vigorous stirring, the
layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl
acetate. The combined organics layers were washed with brine, dried over
anhydrous MgSO4 and evaporate. The reaction crude was purified by flash
chromatography on Et3N pre-treated SiO2 (2.5% v/v) eluting with hexanes/
diethyl ether with increasing polarity, to afford 30 mg of 19a (E isomer,
36% yield) as a yellow oil and a minor amount of Z isomer (5 mg, 6%). E
isomer: [α]D= -7.7 (c 0.38, CHCl3). IR (film): υmax 2927, 2839, 1741,
1697, 1631, 1454 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.04 (s, 3H, CH3), 0.08
(s, 3H, CH3), 0.91 (t, J= 7.6 Hz, 3H, CH3), 0.93 (s, 9H, CH3), 1.21-1.31
(m, 6H, CH2), 1.32-1.41 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.54-1.64 (m, 4H, CH2), 2.20-2.32
(m, 4H, CH2), 2.37-2.43 (m, 2H, CH2), 2.59-2.65 (m, 2H, CH2), 3.66 (s,
3H, CH3), 4.26 (m, 1H, CH), 6.22 (dd, J=16.4, 5.6 Hz, 1H, CH), 6.77 (d,
J= 16.8 Hz, 1H CH) ppm. 13C-NMR(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ -4.5 (CH3), -4.3
(CH3), 9.6 (CH3), 18.5 (C), 23.3 (CH2), 25.1 (CH2), 25.8 (CH2), 26.1 (3C,
CH3), 29.2 (CH2), 29.3 (CH2), 29.4 (CH2), 29.8 (CH2), 31.0 (CH2), 34.0
(CH2), 34.3 (CH2), 51.6 (CH3), 73.9 (CH), 123.5 (CH), 141.1 (2C, CH, C),
163.8 (C), 174.5 (C), 209.8 (C) ppm. MS (ESI (+) H2O: CH3CN): m/z 459
[(M+Na)+, 100%]. HMRS (ESI (+) H2O: CH3CN): calcd for C25H44O4Si:
437.3095; found: 437.3087. Z isomer: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 0.06 (s,
3H, CH3), 0.07 (s, 3H, CH3), 0.89 (s, 9H, CH3), 0.94 (t, J= 7.2 Hz, 3H,
CH3), 1.22-1.41 (m, 8H, CH2), 1.46-1.68 (m, 4H, CH2), 2.20-2.26 (m, 2H,
CH2), 2.29 (t, J=7.6 Hz, 2H, CH2), 2.41-2.45 (m, 2H, CH2), 2.71-2.76(m,
2H, CH2), 3.66 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.59-4.58 (m, 1H, CH), 5.81 (dd, J=12.4, 9.7
Hz, 1H, CH), 6.35 (d, J= 12.4 Hz, 1H CH) ppm.
