$DATUM (S,E)-methyl
7-(2-(3-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)oct-1-enyl)5-oxocyclopent-1-
enyl)heptanoate, 19b. The reaction was carried out employing Barbier type
conditions. A solution of sulfone 14 (183, 0.43 mmol) in 4.5 mL of
anhydrous THF was transferred via cannula under nitrogen to a stirred
solution of the aldehyde 10b (108 mg, 0.43 mmol) in 5.5 mL of anhydrous
THF, and the resulting mixture was cooled to -78 ºC. Then, 1.00 mL of
KHMDS (0.5 M in Toluene, 0.50 mmol) were added at this temperature and,
after 10 min, the reaction mixture was warmed to room temperature and
stirred for 2h. After completion of the reaction, the mixture was
quenched with 4 mL of aqueous saturated NH4Cl solution. After a few
minutes of vigorous stirring, the layers were separated and the aqueous
layer was extracted with ethyl acetate. The combined organics layers were
washed with brine, dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and evaporate. The reaction
crude was purified by flash chromatography on Et3N pre-treated SiO2 (2.5%
v/v) eluting with hexanes/ diethyl ether with increasing polarity, to
afford 45mg of 19b (E isomer, 24% yield) as a yellow oil and a minor
amount of Z isomer (4%). [α]D= +0.3 (c 0.05, CH2Cl2). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 0.04 (s, 3H, CH3), 0.08 (s, 3H, CH3), 0.89 (t, J= 6.8 Hz, 3H,
CH3), 0.93 (s, 9H, CH3), 1.25-1.65 (m, 16H, CH2), 2.25 (t, J= 7.6 Hz, 2H,
CH2), 2.29 (t, J= 7.6 Hz, 2H, CH2), 2.39-2.44 (m, 2H, CH2), 2.61-2.65 (m,
2H, CH2), 3.66 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.28-4.35 (m, 1H, CH), 6.24 (dd, J=15.2, 6
Hz, 1H, CH), 6.76 (d, J= 15.2 Hz, 1H CH) ppm. 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
-4.6 (CH3), -4.3 (CH3), 14.2 (CH3), 18.4 (C), 22.8 (CH2), 23.2 (CH2),
24.9 (CH2), 25.1(CH2), 25.8 (CH2), 26.0 (3C, CH3), 29.1 (CH2), 29.2
(CH2), 29.6 (CH2), 32.0 (CH2), 34.0 (CH2), 34.2 (CH2), 38.2 (CH2), 51.6
(CH3), 72.9 (CH), 123.2 (CH), 140.9 (C), 141.5 (CH), 163.8 (C), 174.4
(C), 209.8 (C) ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
