$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Alcohol S29. To a suspension of Ph3P+CH3Br- (645.6 mg, 1.806 mmol) in THF
(3 mL) at 0 °C was added NaHMDS (1.0 M solution in THF, 1.60 mL, 1.60
mmol), and the resultant suspension was stirred at 0 °C for 30 min. To
the resultant suspension at -78 °C was added a solution of methyl ketone
S28 (224.9 mg, 0.3168 mmol) in THF (1.5 mL + 0.5 mL rinse), and the
resultant mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature over a period
of 4 h 20 min. The reaction mixture was diluted with saturated aqueous
NH4Cl solution and extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed
with H2O and brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under
reduced pressure. The residue was passed through a short silica gel
column (eluted with 20% EtOAc/hexanes) to give a crude olefin which was
used in the next reaction without further purification. Yield 224.5 mg.
