$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Diol 29. To a suspension of Ph3P+CH3Br- (725.5 mg, 2.031 mmol) in THF (12
mL) at 0 °C was added sodium hexamethyldisilazide (NaHMDS) (1.0 M
solution in THF, 1.9 mL, 1.9 mmol), and the resultant suspension was
stirred at 0 °C for 30 min. To the resultant suspension at -78 °C was
added a solution of ketone S20 (499.1 mg, 0.4636 mmol) in THF (3.0 mL + 2
× 1.0 mL rinse), and the reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 2 h.
The reaction mixture was diluted with saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution
and extracted with EtOAc. The organic layer was washed with H2O and
brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography (silica gel,
20% EtOAc/hexanes) to give exo-olefin 28 containing some impurities,
which was used in the next reaction without purification. 28.
