$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method D. A solution of allyl sulfone 16 (250
mg, 1.0 mmol) in DMF/TDA-1 = 3:1 (v/v) (10 mL, 0.1 M) was cooled to -60
°C, and KN(TMS)2 (0.6 M solution in toluene) (1.83 mL, 1.1 mmol) was
added dropwise within 10 s. The resulting mixture was stirred at -60 °C
for 2 min, and aldehyde 12c (131 μL, 1.1 mmol) in DMF (0.2 mL) was added
dropwise. The resulting mixture was stirred at -60 °C for 1 h before it
was allowed to warm to rt. After 6 h at rt, the reaction was terminated
and purified using the same protocol as mentioned in method A. The
reaction yielded 13c14 . Table 3, entry 94, Olefin 13s:.15,20, yield 70%.
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 4.25 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H), 4.36 (dd, J = 6.4,
1.1 Hz, 2H*), 4.58 (s, 2H*), 4.63 (s, 2H), 5.97 (dt, J = 12.4, 6.3 Hz,
1H*), 6.39 (dt, J = 15.9, 6.0 Hz, 1H), 6.67 (d, J = 11.2 Hz, 1H*), 6.69
(d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H), 7.21- 7.53 (m, 10H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ
67.1*, 70.9, 72.3, 72.6*, 126.2, 126.7, 127.3*, 127.8, 127.98, 128.04*,
128.4*, 128.6, 128.7, 129.0, 129.1*, 132.0*, 132.7, 136.7*, 136.9,
138.3*, 138.4; IR (film) ν-1 3061, 3026, 2922, 2848, 1494, 1452, 1360,
1112, 1072, 966, 732, 692; MS (FAB) m/z 295 (15) [M + Na]+, 281 (61), 263
(20), 247 (100), 237 (35), 221 (56), 199 (42), 180 (65); HRMS (FAB) m/ z
calcd for C16H16ONa 247.1099, found 247.1097.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, alternative preparation shown, Julia-Silvestre
olefination
